w: 1.~Have thine own way, Lord! Have thine own way! _ Thou art the Pot- ter; I am the clay. _ Mold me and make me af- ter thy will _ While I am wait- ing, yield- ed and still. _ _
w: 2.~Have thine own way, Lord! Have thine own way! _ Search me and try me, Mas- ter, to- day! _ Whit- er than snow, Lord, wash me just now, _ As in thy pre- sence hum- bly I bow. _ _
w: 3.~Have thine own way, Lord! Have thine own way! _ Wound- ed and wear- y, help me, I pray! _ Po- wer— all po- wer— sure- ly is thine! _ Touch me and heal me, Sa- viour di- vine! _ _
w: 4.~Have thine own way, Lord! Have thine own way! _ Hold o'er my be- ing ab- so- lute sway! _ Fill with thy Spi- rit till all shall see _ Christ on- ly, al- ways, liv- ing in me! _ _
